{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"densityContour"},{"type":"text","value":" estimates a two-dimensional density field after the chart\nresolves its positional scales and inner bounds. Import it from the optional\nspatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { densityContour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/density'\n\nconst mark = densityContour(penguins, {\n  x: 'billLength',\n  y: 'billDepth',\n  bandwidth: 18,\n  thresholds: [0.0004, 0.0008, 0.0012, 0.0016, 0.002, 0.0024],\n  fill: '#2563eb',\n  fillOpacity: 0.16,\n  stroke: '#1e3a8a',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function densityContour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DensityContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never, InferredX, InferredY>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark contributes x/y and derived color domains but intentionally emits no\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":" interaction candidates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source horizontal observation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source vertical observation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Independent density-estimator group"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"weight"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observation weight"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bandwidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"20"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gaussian-kernel bandwidth in final CSS pixels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Density-grid cell size in final CSS pixels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thresholds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Iterable<number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"20"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approximate shared level count or exact density levels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<DensityContourDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived value sent to the color scale; never an estimator group"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour stroke"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour stroke dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whole-contour opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contour enter, update, and exit motion"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bandwidth"},{"type":"text","value":" must be nonnegative and finite. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSize"},{"type":"text","value":" must be at least one;\nthe D3 estimator rounds it down to a supported power of two. A numeric\nthreshold count must be a positive integer. Exact thresholds use weighted\nobservations per CSS pixel squared, the native unit of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3-contour"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"resolved-estimation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved estimation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete x/y pairs establish the positional domains. The mark maps them\nthrough the final scales, estimates inside the final plot rectangle, and clips\nthe output there. Resizing or changing margins can change the contours even\nwhen the semantic domains are fixed. Scale inversion is not required."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" runs one estimator per group. Numeric threshold counts resolve\nto one shared set of levels using the maximum across every group, so levels\nremain comparable. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":" affects presentation only and never partitions the\nestimator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing or unmappable x/y pairs and zero or nonfinite weights contribute\nnothing. Finite signed weights are passed to the estimator. Every rendered\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DensityContourDatum<TDatum>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"density"},{"type":"text","value":", the native threshold value;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"},{"type":"text","value":", the explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" value or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":", the contributing input rows for that estimator group; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":", their original input indexes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"geometry-and-interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Geometry and interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3-geo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A contour can have several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a\ncentroid focus target or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark when\nindividual observations should own focus and tooltips."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"resolved-estimation","text":"Resolved estimation","level":2},{"id":"geometry-and-interaction","text":"Geometry and interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`densityContour` estimates a two-dimensional density field after the chart\nresolves its positional scales and inner bounds. Import it from the optional\nspatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel.\n\n```ts\nimport { densityContour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/density'\n\nconst mark = densityContour(penguins, {\n  x: 'billLength',\n  y: 'billDepth',\n  bandwidth: 18,\n  thresholds: [0.0004, 0.0008, 0.0012, 0.0016, 0.002, 0.0024],\n  fill: '#2563eb',\n  fillOpacity: 0.16,\n  stroke: '#1e3a8a',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction densityContour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DensityContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never, InferredX, InferredY>\n```\n\nThe mark contributes x/y and derived color domains but intentionally emits no\n`ChartPoint` interaction candidates.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                         | Default          | Meaning                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`               | Required         | Source horizontal observation                                   |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`               | Required         | Source vertical observation                                     |\n| `z`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                 | `null` group     | Independent density-estimator group                             |\n| `weight`                                          | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                   | `1`              | Observation weight                                              |\n| `bandwidth`                                       | `number`                                     | `20`             | Gaussian-kernel bandwidth in final CSS pixels                   |\n| `cellSize`                                        | `number`                                     | `4`              | Density-grid cell size in final CSS pixels                      |\n| `thresholds`                                      | `number \\| Iterable<number>`                 | `20`             | Approximate shared level count or exact density levels          |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<DensityContourDatum, ChartKey?>`    | `group`          | Derived value sent to the color scale; never an estimator group |\n| `fill`                                            | `VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>` | Resolved color   | Contour fill                                                    |\n| `stroke`                                          | `VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>` | None             | Contour stroke                                                  |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                     | Renderer default | Contour presentation                                            |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                     | None             | Contour stroke dash pattern                                     |\n| `opacity`                                         | `number`                                     | Renderer default | Whole-contour opacity                                           |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                     | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                                  |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']`    | None             | Contour enter, update, and exit motion                          |\n\n`bandwidth` must be nonnegative and finite. `cellSize` must be at least one;\nthe D3 estimator rounds it down to a supported power of two. A numeric\nthreshold count must be a positive integer. Exact thresholds use weighted\nobservations per CSS pixel squared, the native unit of `d3-contour`.\n\n## Resolved estimation\n\nComplete x/y pairs establish the positional domains. The mark maps them\nthrough the final scales, estimates inside the final plot rectangle, and clips\nthe output there. Resizing or changing margins can change the contours even\nwhen the semantic domains are fixed. Scale inversion is not required.\n\nAn explicit `z` runs one estimator per group. Numeric threshold counts resolve\nto one shared set of levels using the maximum across every group, so levels\nremain comparable. `color` affects presentation only and never partitions the\nestimator.\n\nMissing or unmappable x/y pairs and zero or nonfinite weights contribute\nnothing. Finite signed weights are passed to the estimator. Every rendered\n`DensityContourDatum<TDatum>` contains:\n\n- `density`, the native threshold value;\n- `group`, the explicit `z` value or `null`;\n- `source`, the contributing input rows for that estimator group; and\n- `sourceIndexes`, their original input indexes.\n\nPresentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array.\n\n## Geometry and interaction\n\nEach level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n`d3-geo`.\n\nA contour can have several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a\ncentroid focus target or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark when\nindividual observations should own focus and tooltips.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Density Contour Mark\ndescription: Reference for responsive point-density contours, thresholds, grouping, weights, source lineage, and structured multipolygon output.\n---\n\n`densityContour` estimates a two-dimensional density field after the chart\nresolves its positional scales and inner bounds. Import it from the optional\nspatial subpath; it is not included in the root or universal barrel.\n\n```ts\nimport { densityContour } from '@tanstack/charts/spatial/density'\n\nconst mark = densityContour(penguins, {\n  x: 'billLength',\n  y: 'billDepth',\n  bandwidth: 18,\n  thresholds: [0.0004, 0.0008, 0.0012, 0.0016, 0.002, 0.0024],\n  fill: '#2563eb',\n  fillOpacity: 0.16,\n  stroke: '#1e3a8a',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction densityContour<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DensityContourOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<never, never, never, InferredX, InferredY>\n```\n\nThe mark contributes x/y and derived color domains but intentionally emits no\n`ChartPoint` interaction candidates.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                         | Default          | Meaning                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`               | Required         | Source horizontal observation                                   |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`               | Required         | Source vertical observation                                     |\n| `z`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                 | `null` group     | Independent density-estimator group                             |\n| `weight`                                          | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                   | `1`              | Observation weight                                              |\n| `bandwidth`                                       | `number`                                     | `20`             | Gaussian-kernel bandwidth in final CSS pixels                   |\n| `cellSize`                                        | `number`                                     | `4`              | Density-grid cell size in final CSS pixels                      |\n| `thresholds`                                      | `number \\| Iterable<number>`                 | `20`             | Approximate shared level count or exact density levels          |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<DensityContourDatum, ChartKey?>`    | `group`          | Derived value sent to the color scale; never an estimator group |\n| `fill`                                            | `VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>` | Resolved color   | Contour fill                                                    |\n| `stroke`                                          | `VisualChannel<DensityContourDatum, string>` | None             | Contour stroke                                                  |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                     | Renderer default | Contour presentation                                            |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                     | None             | Contour stroke dash pattern                                     |\n| `opacity`                                         | `number`                                     | Renderer default | Whole-contour opacity                                           |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                     | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                                  |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<never>['motion']`    | None             | Contour enter, update, and exit motion                          |\n\n`bandwidth` must be nonnegative and finite. `cellSize` must be at least one;\nthe D3 estimator rounds it down to a supported power of two. A numeric\nthreshold count must be a positive integer. Exact thresholds use weighted\nobservations per CSS pixel squared, the native unit of `d3-contour`.\n\n## Resolved estimation\n\nComplete x/y pairs establish the positional domains. The mark maps them\nthrough the final scales, estimates inside the final plot rectangle, and clips\nthe output there. Resizing or changing margins can change the contours even\nwhen the semantic domains are fixed. Scale inversion is not required.\n\nAn explicit `z` runs one estimator per group. Numeric threshold counts resolve\nto one shared set of levels using the maximum across every group, so levels\nremain comparable. `color` affects presentation only and never partitions the\nestimator.\n\nMissing or unmappable x/y pairs and zero or nonfinite weights contribute\nnothing. Finite signed weights are passed to the estimator. Every rendered\n`DensityContourDatum<TDatum>` contains:\n\n- `density`, the native threshold value;\n- `group`, the explicit `z` value or `null`;\n- `source`, the contributing input rows for that estimator group; and\n- `sourceIndexes`, their original input indexes.\n\nPresentation accessors receive this derived datum and the complete rendered\ncontour array.\n\n## Geometry and interaction\n\nEach level is one structured scene area containing all disconnected polygons\nand holes. SVG, Canvas, React Native SVG, hit geometry, gradients, and clipping\nconsume the same rings; the mark does not author SVG path strings or depend on\n`d3-geo`.\n\nA contour can have several disconnected regions, and an aggregate centroid\ncan fall outside all of them. The mark therefore does not manufacture a\ncentroid focus target or tooltip datum. Layer an interactive source mark when\nindividual observations should own focus and tooltips.\n"}
